<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">butcher</ansi>

Cut meat, bone, sinew, fat and the rest from a carcass.

  <ansi fg="command">butcher <corpse></ansi>     (also <ansi fg="command">carve</ansi>)

A knife takes the meat, sinew and gut. Bone and fat need a <ansi fg="yellow">cleaver</ansi>; horn,
antler, tusk, fangs and claws need a <ansi fg="yellow">bone saw</ansi>. Whatever you have no tool
for is left behind. Rare parts such as fangs, glands and organs are only
found if you notice them: <ansi fg="yellow">Perception</ansi> decides that.

Butchering is driven by <ansi fg="yellow">Strength</ansi> and <ansi fg="yellow">Dexterity</ansi>, then your tools, then a
little <ansi fg="yellow">salvage</ansi> skill. A strong butcher gets more meat. A carcass that has lain
too long has no meat worth taking.

Butcher <ansi fg="yellow">after</ansi> you skin, or the hide is ruined. Meat and organs rot within a
couple of days: smoke or salt them at a cooking fire, or sell them to a cook.

